[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 359,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 159,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56196,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 159,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Embryonal sarcoma of the liver is a malignant hepatic neoplasm of children, composed of heterogeneous undifferentiated mesenchymal cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:41:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 360,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 160,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56197,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 160,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8991/3 Embryonal sarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:41:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 361,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 161,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56198,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 161,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>XH42Q2 Embryonal sarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:41:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 362,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 162,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56199,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 162,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Acceptable:</em> undifferentiated embryonal sarcoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> malignant mesenchymoma of the liver.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-05-03T10:10:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 363,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 163,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56200,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 163,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:41:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 364,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 164,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56201,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 164,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Embryonal sarcoma usually arises in the right hepatic lobe {3791152; 24210186}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:41:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 365,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 165,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56202,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 165,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients often present with abdominal distension, pain, fever, and weight loss; hepatic rupture with haemoperitoneum is uncommon {208754}. Leukocytosis and elevated serum alkaline phosphatase are common. Invasion of the inferior vena cava with extension to the right atrium may be observed {1702267}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:41:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 366,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 166,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56203,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 166,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Embryonal sarcoma is rare, although it is the most common malignant hepatic mesenchymal neoplasm in the paediatric population. Children aged 5&ndash;15&nbsp;years are typically affected, with no sex predilection {208754; 27781381}; presentation in adulthood is rare {18361435}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:41:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 367,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 167,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56204,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 167,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Embryonal sarcoma is sporadic. Rarely, transformation from mesenchymal hamartoma has been reported {20925497}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:41:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 368,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 168,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56205,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 168,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:41:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 375,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 207,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56206,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 207,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Embryonal sarcoma is well circumscribed but unencapsulated. Tumours are large (10&ndash;30&nbsp;cm). The cut surface is heterogeneous, with alternating solid, fleshy, and mucoid areas and foci of cystic degeneration, necrosis, and haemorrhage {208754}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:41:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 369,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 169,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56207,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 169,
        "headingText": "<p>The tumour is typically composed of variably spindled, stellate, and pleomorphic giant cells loosely arranged in a myxoid stroma; fibrotic areas with solid, fascicular, or storiform growth may be observed {208754; 1702267}. Cytoplasmic PAS-positive eosinophilic hyaline (lysosomal) globules in giant cells are a characteristic finding {208754}. Mitotic activity (including atypical mitoses) is easily detected. Peripheral entrapment of bile ducts is often seen, as is extramedullary haematopoiesis. Rare cases associated with mesenchymal hamartoma have been reported {9331300; 11779051}.</p>\r\n<p>Embryonal sarcoma shows no specific immunophenotype. Variable, often limited expression of keratins, desmin, and MSA may be seen {1702267; 17378682; 16785789}; a subset of cases are positive for glypican-3 (GPC3) {21937079}. The tumour cells are negative for EMA, Hep&nbsp;Par-1 (CPS1), AFP, myogenin, and MYOD1 {17378682}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-23T15:42:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 370,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 170,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56208,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 170,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:41:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 371,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 171,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56209,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 171,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Embryonal sarcoma typically shows a complex karyotype {11376805}. The t(11;19)(q13;q13.4) characteristic of mesenchymal hamartoma has been detected in several cases {17311249}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:41:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 374,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 174,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56210,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 174,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> spindled, stellate, and pleomorphic giant cells loosely arranged in a myxoid stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:41:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 372,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 172,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56211,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 172,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:41:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 373,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 173,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 56212,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 218,
        "headingId": 173,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Although embryonal sarcoma of the liver may pursue an aggressive clinical course, with metastases to the lung and peritoneum, patients with surgically resectable tumours often have a favourable outcome {24210186; 26925712; 27427850}. Tumour size &gt;&nbsp;15&nbsp;cm is an adverse prognostic indicator {27781381}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:41:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]